Scenario: View Blog Entry Via Read Post Button
	End users should be able to view the top blog entry via the Read Post button.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I click on the Read Post button
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry

Scenario: View Blog Entries Via Blog Links
	End users should be able to view the blog entries via the Blog Entry links.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I click on the blog entry in the position "1" in the blog index
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on the blog entry in the position "3" in the blog index
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on the blog entry in the position "5" in the blog index
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on the blog entry in the position "7" in the blog index
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on the blog entry in the position "9" in the blog index
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry

Scenario: View Blog Entries Via Customer Experience Featured Links
	End users should be able to view the blog entries via the Customer Experience Featured Links.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I click on a featured blog entry link located in position "1" under the "Customer Experience" category
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on a featured blog entry link located in position "2" under the "Customer Experience" category
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry
	When I go to the www page with the url "blog"
	And I click on a featured blog entry link located in position "3" under the "Customer Experience" category
	Then I should be able to view the content of the blog entry

